10. ANONYMOUS DATA COLLECTION — USE MEANS CONSENT
   (a) The Software collects a limited, anonymous set of data, used only to
       understand usage and ad performance: ad impressions / views / clicks; one
       "new user" record when the Software first runs on a device; an online
       heartbeat every 5 minutes while it is running, used to count how many
       people are online right now; and a coarse region (country / province /
       city) resolved by the server from the IP of the network request. These
       records contain only a randomly generated device id, the version, the UI
       language, a timestamp and that coarse region. Raw IP addresses are never
       written to the statistics database.
   (b) The Software never collects note text or images, file paths or names,
